    "text_1315676503": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Jun 10 2026 18:10:28 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\">Equipment is crucial</span></span></h2>\n<p>When Hall was on the design team at her new facility, purchasing Stryker’s Neptune Waste Management System was non-negotiable. The Neptune System helps protect staff from biohazardous fluid exposure and streamlines the colonoscopy process because it reduces the need to empty canisters during a procedure.</p>\n<p>Hall says nurses who come to work at the facility are amazed they don’t have to be exposed to the waste, therefore, she believes the Neptune System helps with staff retention. “Too many people don’t know what the options are for GI,” Hall continues. She has introduced colleagues at other facilities to the innovative technology of a constantly closed system, as well.</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Jun 10 2026 18:11:28 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
